Z||000010||terryk||11-13-2001||01:11 AM||||"your legs are the first line of defense in an accident"<P>With VW buses we used to say "your feet are the first to arrive at the scene of the accident."<P>I'll ask my dad about the engines. I believe the coupe was a 1 cyl and sedan was a dual, but that's been a long time. They were amazingly nibble, but my mom drove them like they were Grand Nationals and roasted one of the engines twice. Pops took a dim view of that and finally put her in an Olds Super 98 with a 394....||||reg||1
Z||000011||Slammed Fiero||11-13-2001||01:27 AM||||haha<P>Don't know if I have mentioned htis before , But I inherited a 1956 Isetta from my grandfather.<P>What a thrill to drive. The motor has been swapped out in mine for a more reliable motor cycle motor , (600cc) Just a blast to drive , has one gauge (volts) 3spd tranny , with reverse, has 3 brakes , 2 on the front , and one on the rear in the transmission case (mine is 4 wheeled) <P>The brake resivoir is right at your feet , slding canvas sunroof.. Just a blast to drive.<P><BR>JM ||||reg||1
